# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Postflare — environment template
#
# This file contains ONLY non-secret placeholders and documentation.
# NEVER commit real secrets. The only manually configured application
# encryption secret is ENCRYPTION_KEY, and it lives in a Cloudflare Worker
# secret (or .dev.vars for local development), never in this file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Copy this file to `.dev.vars` for local development and fill in the value.
# Generate a secure key with:
#
#   openssl rand -base64 32
#
# ENCRYPTION_KEY is a base64-encoded 32-byte key used to AES-256-GCM encrypt
# every third-party platform credential stored by the application.
ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# Optional: when set, a fresh local installation will be seeded with this
# user during `npm run dev` (used only for local smoke-testing convenience).
# SEED_ADMIN_EMAIL=
# SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD=